The interesting part of this message is entirely in the headers:

  * Adjacent encoded words that must be joined with no space between
    them (the Subject and the Cc display name both do this).
  * Two different charsets inside one header field.
  * A folded Subject where the continuation line begins with an
    encoded word.
  * Display names in Q and B encoding, plus one that needs neither.

The body itself is unremarkable ASCII so that decoding failures are
unambiguously header-side.
